<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for June 17.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for June 17.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc has announced the following forecasts and data for UK natural gas in the period June 15 to 17.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>June 15 (actual)156 mcm, 36 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>June 16 (forecast) 159 mcm, 37 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>June 17 (forecast) 159 mcm, 37 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>(SNT = seasonal normal temperature)</p>
<p>June 15 (actual) 12.4 Celsius, SNT 15.5 Celsius</p>
<p>June 16 (forecast) 13.9 Celsius, SNT 15.6 Celsius</p>
<p>June 17 (forecast) 15.1 Celsius, SNT 15.7 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no interruption called for Monday, with none expected on Tuesday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
